                size    1
                default { 3 }
                range   { 1 65 }
                help    "From this scattering event on, paths that carry little light are ended by chance and the survivors weighted up: the image stays the same, deep bounces cost less and get a little noisier. Higher values keep more paths alive (less noise in deep indirect light and in many layers of glass, longer renders); a value above Max Ray Depth turns the roulette off."
